{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Establish a consistent, observable error-handling convention (remediation-led) + enable BLE001\n\n## Context\n\nA codebase-health audit (joe-janitor, 2026-06-24) found ~199 `except Exception`/`except BaseException`\nsites in `src/rebar` (~96 already `# noqa: BLE001`-justified, ~100 unguarded), ~104 scattered\n`print(..., file=sys.stderr)` diagnostics, and `logging` used in only a handful of modules with **no\nhandler configured anywhere**. Each agent session invented its own swallow style (`pass`, silent\nfallback, ad-hoc stderr print), so unintended swallows hide real failures with no operator signal — a\ncross-session-inconsistency smell.\n\n**This epic is remediation-led: the primary deliverable is remediated code that SETS the pattern, not a\ndesign-decision document.** The convention is established by an exemplar remediation (working code other\nbatches copy) plus a CI lint gate, not by prose. This was decided after researching rebar's actual peers\n(basic-memory, the `modelcontextprotocol/servers` reference servers, mcp-atlassian) and the MCP framework\nitself — the chosen convention is deliberately boring and uses no novel/rarely-used elements.\n\n## The convention (demonstrated by the exemplar, enforced by lint)\n\n- **MCP surface:** don't catch-and-return error dicts — just `raise`; the MCP framework converts a raised\n  exception into an `isError` tool result and keeps the connection alive. Use `ToolError` for intentional,\n  clean client-facing messages (e.g. `ConcurrencyError`, validation).\n- **CLI surface:** a base `RebarError` caught at the boundary maps to an exit code (already in place;\n  `ConcurrencyError` -> exit 10).\n- **Library:** named `logging.getLogger(__name__)` under the `rebar` root + a `NullHandler` in\n  `__init__.py`; the CLI and MCP entrypoints each install a **stderr** `StreamHandler`.\n- **Best-effort case:** inline narrow-and-log — **no shared helper** (peers don't have one; a helper would\n  be novel). `try/except <type>: logger.warning(..., exc_info=True)`.\n- **Terminal state = observability floor:** every broad catch must either log with `exc_info` OR carry a\n  justified `# noqa: BLE001` (reason string required). Narrowing is opportunistic, with tests; fail-open /\n  body-inspecting / public-API sites stay broad-but-logged.\n- **Enforcement:** ruff **BLE001** (blind-except) and **T201** (print, scoped: banned in library/core/MCP,\n  allowed in the CLI presentation layer) enabled in CI, gated behind a *shrinking* `per-file-ignores`\n  allowlist (the existing `.github/module-size-allowlist.txt` strangler pattern).\n\n## stdout is sacred (the load-bearing constraint)\n\nCLI *data* `print(json.dumps(...))` on stdout is a machine contract (the reconciler `json.loads` it at\n`reconcile.py:472`) and MCP-over-stdio reserves stdout for JSON-RPC framing. Only **stderr diagnostics**\nmigrate to the logger; stdout data prints stay.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The logging substrate exists (named loggers + `NullHandler` + stderr handler at both entrypoints) and\n      a stdout-purity contract test guards the CLI data contract.\n- [ ] An exemplar package (`llm/plan_review/`) is fully remediated to the convention and is the reference\n      others copy; BLE001 + scoped T201 are enabled with a shrinking allowlist.\n- [ ] The ~100 unguarded broad-except sites are remediated to the observability floor in batches (log with\n      `exc_info` or justified `# noqa: BLE001`); no silent `except ...: pass` remains without justification.\n- [ ] Where opportunistic narrowing surfaced a previously-hidden bug, it is fixed with a regression test;\n      if no batch surfaced one, the close-out records that explicitly (so AC4 is not vacuously satisfied).\n- [ ] The convention is durably documented in `CLAUDE.md` / a contributing doc (not only in the exemplar\n      code + lint), so the rationale (raise-don't-catch on MCP, stdout-sacred, noqa-with-reason) survives.\n- [ ] The allowlist is emptied; `make lint` + the full test suite pass; child tasks are parented here with\n      file-impact set.\n- [ ] One observable, lint-enforced way to do error handling across rebar's library / CLI / MCP surfaces.\n- [ ] Failures that used to vanish silently are now observable on a stderr logger; `KeyboardInterrupt` /\n- [ ] A future joe-janitor audit finds no unguarded blind-except cluster; new unguarded blind-excepts / stray"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007103557630001,"uuid":"bd53a275-9f69-4910-84ef-eeecdbfc502c"}